Unified firmware physics-engine tests.

The Unity tests link the real `PhysicsEngine.cpp` and cover the Copeland
ZP29K6E-PFV performance-chart map, each refrigerant's CoolProp-derived PT curve
and inverse lookup, off-cycle/update pressure behavior, pressure ramping,
airflow-fault effects, and telemetry bounds. The compressor chart data is
for R-410A at 60 Hz, 20 F superheat, and 15 F subcooling; its nominal tolerance
is +/-5%. Map inputs beyond the published chart range clamp to the nearest
chart edge. R-454B uses the Copeland YA31K1E-PFV chart 99949-230 (3-ton, 20 F superheat,
15 F subcooling, current @ 230 V, +/-5%) for both trainer types; its test checks
published and interpolated points. R-32 likewise uses the Copeland YP31K1T-PFV
chart 118323-230 on both trainer types, and R-410A uses the ZP29K6E-PFV chart on both.
Other refrigerants continue to use the engine's
existing scaling factors with the R-410A compressor map. The refrigerant PT tables likewise run
without CoolProp on the ESP32. Fault coverage checks that blower loss trips the
low-pressure switch near its trip threshold, holds it until pressure recovers,
and that condenser-fan loss raises liquid pressure during cooling. Build tests
without uploading using the command below. Running them requires a dedicated
ESP32 test board.

Run the native tests and verify the offline-generated CoolProp table with:

```bash
pio test -e physics_test --without-uploading
python tools/validate-refrigerant-pressure.py
```
